      "why": "The payload segment's last character sets bits that base64url decoding discards, so two different strings decode to the same bytes. A lax decoder would hand the two of them the same claims while the signature covers only one, which is how a token gets to mean different things to different readers. Rejected as malformed, before any crypto is spent."
